{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","hash":"f15c26c4e6a4543a45d7c773d6e9e41b0b3d87d726e3bb917eb431b6f23540e6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Checking board 5 and 5b's exact wording before drawing the card."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XCHeqGbzwDBza4V6xNkPzF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad/artifact-files/e4519567-125b-4ce3-a8a6-d33f8afb3449/project && ls | grep -i calib; for f in calibration-05*; do echo \"== $f\"; sed -e 's/<[^>]*>/ /g' \"$f\" | tr -s ' \\n' | head -c 3000; echo; done","description":"Read board 5 and 5b text"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","hash":"c595efc307efc9b2617b6f60bed0708cb14f9cb6be87b528bd6e70c92bb5c6fd","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XCHeqGbzwDBza4V6xNkPzF","type":"tool_result","content":"calibration-01-entry-points.dc.html\ncalibration-02-symptom-in-project-chat.dc.html\ncalibration-03-confirm-from-menu.dc.html\ncalibration-04-test-project.dc.html\ncalibration-05-reading-the-tower.dc.html\ncalibration-05b-result-card.dc.html\ncalibration-06-saved.dc.html\ncalibration-07-reopened-later.dc.html\ncalibration-08-home.dc.html\n== calibration-05-reading-the-tower.dc.html\n \n \n \n \n 5 · Reading the print \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nbody{margin:0}\n \n \n 5 · Reading the print The person is the sensor: a photo of the tower, with the numbers readable, sent as the app sends a photo, the picture above the words. The agent names the block and why, then proposes one write. Nothing here is a temperature widget: the proposal is a Chat/Tool Activity card whose rows are the ordinary settings preview (the setting, old → new, and the preset it is saved as), filled from the test’s declaration. The outcome of every test is the same thing, a new preset; nothing is written until “Save preset”. Temperature tower for Gray PETG Setup summary Current Temperature tower, Gray PETG on MK4 0.20mm Standard · Gray PETG 240 → 210 °C in 5 °C blocks; read the cleanest block 48 min 11 g All settings Here it is. Worked for 12s · 1 action 225 °C is the cleanest block: no hairs between the posts and the bridges are straight. 230 °C shows fine hairs; 220 °C and below look dull and the layers bond less well. I would set Gray PETG to 225 °C on this printer. Save 225 °C as a new filament preset New preset · Gray PETG · MK4 calibrated Nozzle temperature 240 → 225 °C Gray PETG itself is unchanged Save preset Pick another block Ask about this print or request a change… Claude Opus 5.5 Thinking: Medium Send \n \n \nclass Component extends DCLogic {\nrenderVals() { return {}; }\n}\n \n \n \n\n== calibration-05b-result-card.dc.html\n \n \n \n \n 5b · One result card, any test \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nbody{margin:0}\n \n \n 5b · One result card, any test The card on board 5 is one instance of a single shape: a Chat/Tool Activity card with three status rows and the two action buttons the component already has. Its slots are the value and unit the test produces, the preset scope the setting belongs to (filament, process or printer), the base preset and printer that name the copy, the setting with its old and new values from the settings preview, and the word for what the person picks. A second calibration on the same base updates the same copy rather than adding a name. Tests whose result lives on the machine (Bambu’s measured pressure advance, input shaping) do not produce this card. The shape · every slot comes from the test’s declaration or the settings preview Save {value} as a new {scope} preset New preset · {base} · {printer} calibrated {setting} {old} → {new} {base} itself is unchanged Save preset Pick another {step} Temperature tower · filament preset Save 225 °C as a new filament preset New preset · Gray PETG · MK4 calibrated Nozzle temperature 240 → 225 °C Gray PETG itself is unchanged Save preset Pick another block Flow ratio · filament preset Save 0.95 as a new filament preset New preset · Gray PETG · MK4 calibrated Flow ratio 0.98 → 0.95 Gray PETG itself is unchanged Save preset Pick another tile VFA speed · process preset Save 120 mm/s as a new process preset New preset · 0.20mm Standard · MK4 calibrated Outer wall speed 200 → 120 mm/s 0.20mm Standard itself is unchanged Save preset Pick another band \n \n \nclass Component extends DCLogic {\nrenderVals() { return {}; }\n}\nShell cwd was reset to C:\\src\\JusPrin","is_error":false}]}}
