{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","hash":"9d21701a6920c16e9734419ff70d8c4206215e4295fc99d26acc93c84cb667b2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ceu5rLTkDpcxGEatuVC3tS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad/artifact-files/e4519567-125b-4ce3-a8a6-d33f8afb3449/project && sed -e 's/<[^>]*>/ /g' calibration-06-saved.dc.html | tr -s ' \\n' | head -c 2500; echo; grep -o 'data-c=\"Chat/[^\"]*\"' calibration-06-saved.dc.html | sort | uniq -c","description":"Read board 6 text and components"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","hash":"216defa5d416e8659d31bbfc89811a7ad9d924ef3bfdd966c9c21355e952404a","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ceu5rLTkDpcxGEatuVC3tS","type":"tool_result","content":" 6 · Saved: the preset to use from now on \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nbody{margin:0}\n \n \n 6 · Saved: the preset to use from now on Every test ends the same way: a new preset, confirmed by the receipt an added printer already gets, with Undo. The app does no switching. The agent tells the person the preset’s name and that it is theirs to pick in the filament chip of whatever they print next; this test project already uses it. The test’s temporary edits are discarded on the way out, so OrcaSlicer’s “keep modified presets?” dialog is not shown. Temperature tower for Gray PETG Setup summary Current Temperature tower, Gray PETG on MK4 0.20mm Standard · Gray PETG 240 → 210 °C in 5 °C blocks; read the cleanest block 48 min 11 g All settings Saved: Gray PETG · MK4 calibrated Filament preset · nozzle temperature 225 °C Undo From now on, pick Gray PETG · MK4 calibrated as the filament whenever you print this spool on the MK4. Nothing switches by itself: this test uses it now, and your other projects keep the filament they have until you change it in the chip. The hairs between the posts should mostly be gone; if some remain after a real print, a retraction test is the next step. Run the flow test next Ask about this print or request a change… Claude Opus 5.5 Thinking: Medium Send \n \n \nclass Component extends DCLogic {\nrenderVals() { return {}; }\n}\n \n \n \n\n      1 data-c=\"Chat/Bubble:Role=Agent\"\n      1 data-c=\"Chat/Receipt\"\n      1 data-c=\"Chat/Reply Choice:State=Normal\"\nShell cwd was reset to C:\\src\\JusPrin","is_error":false}]}}
