r asks of a person who makes that change, or saves it, by hand, in its own words. The patch skips it and applies as sent, so it is yours to settle before applying: go ahead; go ahead and tell the user; or, when the answer is the user's to give (it depends on what the object is for, or it accepts a risk to their printer), ask them first. Its suggestions are the values OrcaSlicer's Yes would set; add them to the patch to accept them.\",\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:1091:         object_schema({{\"scope\", settings_scope}, {\"target\", settings_target}, {\"changes\", changes_input}, {\"persistAs\", persist_as}},\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:1096:         \"Apply an atomic settings patch immediately. Requires the sessionId and revision from a preview of the same scope, target, changes and persistAs; edits to the model since that preview do not matter, a settings change does. A process, filament or printer change is not undone by project Undo; an object override is. With persistAs the preset is saved as well, and savedAs names what it was saved as.\",","is_error":false}]}}
