{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","hash":"db32ea234670ba4352d7c2de670e24e06619590c86086da09c123e5de60c0d06","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013LXDsySVod5cyb141wgtgx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/src/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/calibration && /c/Users/guitest/.local/python-3.13.9/python.exe -c \"\nimport json;m=json.load(open('resources/jusprin/ui/icons/lucide-map.json'));print(m['package'],m['version']);i=m['icons'];print(type(i), (list(i.items())[:3] if isinstance(i,dict) else i[:3]))\"; ls resources/jusprin/ui/icons | head -80 | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; grep -n \"icon\" agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md | head -20","description":"Read the icon map and how icons are added"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","hash":"45c445ca2e306c538101b42960cb85fc1053458451531b26906cfb61945c2fc6","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013LXDsySVod5cyb141wgtgx","type":"tool_result","content":"lucide-static 1.47.0\r\n<class 'dict'> [('arrow-up', 'arrow-up'), ('box', 'box'), ('check', 'check')]\r\nLUCIDE-LICENSE.txt README.md arrow-up.svg box.svg check.svg chevron-down.svg chevron-left.svg chevron-right.svg chevron-up.svg circle-alert.svg circle-check.svg circle-minus.svg circle-play.svg clock.svg close.svg copy.svg download.svg ellipsis.svg eye.svg grid-3x3.svg info.svg layers-3.svg lock-keyhole.svg lock.svg lucide-map.json maximize-2.svg message-circle.svg monitor.svg move.svg package.svg pencil.svg plus.svg printer.svg rotate-ccw.svg rotate-cw.svg search.svg send.svg settings.svg sliders.svg triangle-alert.svg undo-dot.svg upload.svg verify_lucide.py x.svg \n23:The primary expressions are the horizontal lockup, the compact product mark, and the text wordmark. Use the compact mark for application icons and small product contexts.\n116:  - `small`, 4 DIP: standard controls (secondary and icon buttons, fields, the segmented control), matching OrcaSlicer's own controls.\n134:Use the existing native component density and Lucide `v1.47.0` SVG artwork for generic functional icons. Pin the artwork in `resources/jusprin/ui/icons` and use the same SVG geometry in the design artifacts, the React pages, and the native shell; a package or plugin alone is not the cross-surface source of truth. Keep the JusPrin mark and product-specific symbols custom. Functional clarity comes before logo-derived decoration.\n136:- Functional icons: Lucide artwork at 16, 20, or 24 DIP, colored through the surrounding semantic token, with PNG fallback when the platform path requires it. Do not create a separate UI component for each glyph.\n137:- Setup card fact glyphs: 14 DIP from `component.setupCard.iconSize`, the one size below the icon scale. The clock, material, plate, warning, and info glyphs sit inside a row of Label or Metadata text, 14 to 16 DIP tall, and a 16 DIP glyph makes that row taller than its text. The card's disclosure chevron is an ordinary 16 DIP icon. Do not use this size on another surface; it is not a step of the icon scale.\n138:- Agent message box: one box with the `medium` radius, a 1 DIP `border.subtle` inside stroke, and `component.composer` insets (8 DIP padding, 4 DIP between staged files, the field, and the toolbar). The field is Body Small with a 4 DIP inset; it grows a line at a time up to `component.composer.maxLines` (8) and then scrolls, while the toolbar stays visible: the 32 DIP + icon button (or Photo) on the left, Send (`button.primarySmall`, 28 DIP) or Stop (`button.secondarySmall`, 28 DIP) on the right. While the field has the focus the whole box carries the 2 DIP `border.focus` ring. In the app, each + menu choice opens the operating system's file dialog through the host, filtered to that kind. After + come the model and thinking pickers (`button.picker`: 24 DIP, Label, a chevron), which open upward menus no narrower than `component.popover.width`: the model menu lists each set-up provider's models under the provider's name when there is more than one (a provider is added from the Agent settings); the thinking menu lists only the levels the chosen model accepts and is left out when it accepts none. A choice belongs to the chat and applies from its next turn. When the full labels do not fit beside + and Send (the composer measures them, so this follows the labels, not a breakpoint), the thinking picker drops \"Thinking:\" and shows the level alone; if that still does not fit, the model's name is cut with an ellipsis. Both keep their full name as the accessible name and the tooltip. A model menu of more than 12 models opens with the focus in a Field/Search (`component.fieldSearch`: 38 DIP, `small` radius, a 1 DIP `border.subtle` stroke that becomes 2 DIP `border.strong` with the focus) inset 8 DIP from the menu's sides; the menu is then `component.popover.width` wide and its rows scroll under the field. Typing filters on the model or provider name, ignoring case, the first match carries the menu-row hover fill, Up and Down move it, Enter picks it, and Escape clears the field before it closes the menu. A provider with more than 12 models shows its count beside its name while nothing is typed.\n139:- All settings panel (the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas, page \"Current Setup Card\", the four \"All settings\" boards): opened from the setup card's \"All settings\" link, it takes the Agent pane's place under a header of the compact icon button back to the chat, the title in Body Bold and the pane's own toggle. A \"Showing\" row holds the design system's Select (`component.select`: 26 DIP, `small` radius, Body text, a 16 DIP chevron, a 1 DIP `border.subtle` stroke that strengthens on hover and becomes the focus ring when open; its menu is the Menu/Popover under its left edge, as wide as the field) listing the whole project, each plate when there are two or more, and each object; it follows the selection in the 3D view. Under it a Field/Search (\"Search settings\") beside an All / Changed Segmented Control. The presets in use sit in a `surface.subtle` box with the `medium` radius, each filament slot with its Swatch (`component.swatch`, 24 DIP, `small` radius, a 1 DIP `border.subtle` inside stroke). Groups are OrcaSlicer's own pages (Quality, Strength, Speed, Support, Multimaterial, Others, then Filament and Printer) with a 32 DIP header row (16 DIP chevron, Body Small Bold name, Label summary at the right) and rows indented 24 DIP: Body Small name and value on a 28 DIP line, a changed value in Body Small Bold with \"Preset: …\" in Metadata under it. Two or three filament slots stand side by side, one column per slot; more than three go through a slot picker, one at a time. The host reads the whole table in one message (`settings_catalog`, the `all_settings` capability). Only one object's view has anything to press: a Button/Link at the end of a row's note, under the value, where the table marks one — \"Use project value\" under a setting the object, a part, a modifier or a height range sets itself (not a range's own layer height or filament, which define it), and \"Remove\" under its support blockers or enforcers. Each press is one OrcaSlicer undo step of the person's, named for what it did, and the panel redraws from the host's next table (`settings_action`, the `settings_actions` capability).\n147:- Icon button: 32×32 DIP, 16 DIP icon, 4 DIP radius (`component.button.icon`).\n148:- Compact icon target: 26×26 DIP (`component.button.iconCompact`), only for the canvas tool strip and the reset button in a form row, which stands at the field's height.\n159:- Agent-pane collapse: an icon button in the header, left of the overflow button, whose glyph fills its right-hand column while the pane is open and empties it while the pane is closed. Double-clicking the divider closes the pane. Dragging it does not: a drag only sizes the pane and stops at its 320 DIP minimum, so aiming for a narrow pane never takes the conversation off the screen. There is no keyboard shortcut, no animation, and no automatic reopening; the pane is hidden, never destroyed, so its conversation survives. Reopening restores the width it last held.\n161:Every interactive component must define normal, hover, pressed, disabled, focused, success, warning, and error states where relevant. Status must combine color with an icon and plain-language label.\n245:     icons are the `currentColor` SVGs in `resources/jusprin/ui/icons`,\n257:   - `BitmapCache::SetColorReplaces` rewrites the teal in the SVG icon set to\n278:     lockups, monochrome mark, wizard watermark, and window icons under\n321:7. Use the original logo and existing functional icon system.","is_error":false}]}}
