{"parentUuid":"98aff06e-59e9-4c91-b7e2-f403dad25669","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHfPQ2J1bTAAnVQEBj8g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BiZN9nj3doXvVBj5oGSKD3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add resources/jusprin/agent/protocol.json src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin tests/agent tests/jusprin_support tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp && git status --short | grep -v \"^M \\|^A \"; cat > /c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad/msg-board6.txt <<'EOF'\nUndo a saved calibration preset from its receipt\n\nBoard 6: the receipt of a filament preset the person saved from a\nproposal carries Undo, as an added printer's receipt does. For a new copy\nthe project's filament slots that use it take the preset it was made from\nagain and the copy is deleted, in OrcaSlicer's order for deleting a\npreset (cloud deletion queued first; the selected preset and its edits\nkept). For a save into an existing copy, Undo puts that copy's earlier\nvalues back. The receipt then says \"Removed: <name>\" (or \"Undone:\") with\nno button, its note text tells the model, and the Agent's turn starts.\n\nNew IWorkspace::remove_filament_preset (adapter and fake), page message\nundo_receipt, and a change anchor on the document so the edits Undo makes\nfollow its receipt. The thread draws the receipt in place of the change\nrows an approved save and its Undo made, as the board does. The proposal\nnames its preset by Orca's alias, which the receipt repeats.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git commit -q -F /c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad/msg-board6.txt </dev/null 2>/dev/null; git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the board 6 work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_