{"parentUuid":"41f54802-ee22-44ef-9e87-266f7f7e6ede","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31b05e56-dc9c-4fee-8c21-22f2e308b592","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014rFqRapTWJwYpL371Kx1J2","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Title: 7 · The test project, reopened later\nURL: http://127.0.0.1:18431/calibration-07-reopened-later.dc.html\nSource element: <body>\n---\n7 · The test project, reopened later\nOrcaSlicer keeps the tower’s temperature steps only in memory; the saved file has a plain tower. A reopened test says so before the person slices it, keeps its result on record, and offers to regenerate. The pinned card shows it the way the card already shows a stale estimate: the state reads Out of date and the card’s attention block carries the warning.\nTemperature tower for Gray PETG\nSetup summary\nOut of date\nTemperature tower, Gray PETG on MK4\n0.20mm Standard · Gray PETG\n240 → 210 °C in 5 °C blocks; result 225 °C saved\n48 min\n11 g\nTemperature steps not kept in the file\nAll settings\nOpened from Home · generated 21 Oct 2026 · result 225 °C saved\nThis tower was generated on 21 October. Reopening it does not bring back the per-block temperatures, so slicing it now would print the whole tower at 240 °C. I can regenerate it with the same range if you want to print it again.\nRegenerate tower\nJust look at it\nAsk about this print or request a change…\nClaude Opus 5.5\nThinking: Medium\nSend"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nTab Context:\n- Executed on tabId: seed\n- Available tabs:\n  • tabId seed: \"7 · The test project, reopened later\" (\"http://127.0.0.1:18431/calibration-07-reopened-later.dc.html\")"}]}]},"uuid":"afe898c8-fd48-470d-9033-4bad2615552e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:01:26.303Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Title: 7 · The test project, reopened later\nURL: http://127.0.0.1:18431/calibration-07-reopened-later.dc.html\nSource element: <body>\n---\n7 · The test project, reopened later\nOrcaSlicer keeps the tower’s temperature steps only in memory; the saved file has a plain tower. A reopened test says so before the person slices it, keeps its result on record, and offers to regenerate. The pinned card shows it the way the card already shows a stale estimate: the state reads Out of date and the card’s attention block carries the warning.\nTemperature tower for Gray PETG\nSetup summary\nOut of date\nTemperature tower, Gray PETG on MK4\n0.20mm Standard · Gray PETG\n240 → 210 °C in 5 °C blocks; result 225 °C saved\n48 min\n11 g\nTemperature steps not kept in the file\nAll settings\nOpened from Home · generated 21 Oct 2026 · result 225 °C saved\nThis tower was generated on 21 October. Reopening it does not bring back the per-block temperatures, so slicing it now would print the whole tower at 240 °C. I can regenerate it with the same range if you want to print it again.\nRegenerate tower\nJust look at it\nAsk about this print or request a change…\nClaude Opus 5.5\nThinking: Medium\nSend"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nTab Context:\n- Executed on tabId: seed\n- Available tabs:\n  • tabId seed: \"7 · The test project, reopened later\" (\"http://127.0.0.1:18431/calibration-07-reopened-later.dc.html\")"}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"41f54802-ee22-44ef-9e87-266f7f7e6ede","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"claude/calibration","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
