{"parentUuid":"72444ed3-2f6b-4425-8544-fe6b54451930","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHiMRPRuDKuEsCQ5c1nJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017NpxvJcrtgds5rpqjKoiq3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 30,50p /c/Users/guitest/Downloads/calibration-handoff.md; sed -n 155,175p /c/Users/guitest/Downloads/calibration-handoff.md","description":"Read the handoff's notes on reopening"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1188,"cache_read_input_tokens":392905,"output_tokens":146,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1188,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":146,"cache_read_input_tokens":392905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1188},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017NpxvJcrtgds5rpqjKoiq3":{"command":"sed -n 30,50p /c/Users/guitest/Downloads/calibration-handoff.md; sed -n 155,175p /c/Users/guitest/Downloads/calibration-handoff.md","description":"Read the handoff's notes on reopening"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgHiMR467dsTxH2jBgzmu","requestRef":"8dccada9-6e8f-4344-9732-916583d838f7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"70596c2c-8c45-46c2-addd-015147fb61d9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:01:41.661Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"claude/calibration","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
{"parentUuid":"70596c2c-8c45-46c2-addd-015147fb61d9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31b05e56-dc9c-4fee-8c21-22f2e308b592","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017NpxvJcrtgds5rpqjKoiq3","type":"tool_result","content":"## 3. Facts verified in the code (read, not run)\n\n1. **Every OrcaSlicer generator replaces the open project and edits project-wide presets.** `Plater::calib_pa`,\n   `calib_temp`, `calib_flowrate`, `calib_max_vol_speed`, `calib_retraction`, `calib_VFA`, the input-shaping pair and\n   `Calib_Cornering` (`src/slic3r/GUI/Plater.cpp` from about line 12677) each call `new_project()` and then write to\n   `preset_bundle->prints/filaments/printers.get_edited_preset().config`. Plates have no presets of their own, so a\n   test on a plate of an existing project would change every other plate. Do not try.\n2. **The test's parameters are runtime-only.** The generator stores them on the current plate's `Print` with\n   `set_calib_params` (`Print.hpp:1089`); `GCode.cpp` reads them per layer (temperature at line 4697). Nothing writes\n   them to the 3MF, and loading a project resets the mode to none at `Plater.cpp:5891`. A saved temperature tower,\n   reopened, slices as a plain tower at one temperature. The pressure-advance pattern is the exception: its per-layer\n   commands go into the plate's custom G-code, which the 3MF does save. The PA pattern also hard-codes the first\n   plate's origin (`Plater.cpp:12814`).\n3. **OrcaSlicer already treats one outcome as a new preset.** The Bambu wizard's save page writes flow results as a\n   filament preset named \"<filament> Flow Rate Calibrated\" (`CalibrationWizardSavePage.cpp:37`). Its pressure-advance\n   results go to the machine, not a preset. The SoftFever dialogs (`calib_dlg.cpp`) save nothing: the person types\n   the value into a preset by hand.\n4. **Saving a copy already exists and selects the copy.** `settings_apply_patch` with `persistAs` saves through\n   Orca's own `Tab::save_preset` and asserts the copy is now selected\n   (`Workspace/OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:3356-3369`); the result carries `saved_as`. A stock preset cannot be\n   overwritten and the preview says so with `read_only_preset` and a suggested copy name (`check_persist`, line\n(`Dialog` in `AgentUI/src/components/ChatNavigation.tsx`, `.chat-dialog` in `styles.css`): a web dialog, not\nOrca's `MessageDialog` and not a new native dialog. Kenneth decided this on 2026-10-21 (relayed from the\nplacement-brainstorm session) so that board 3 is matched exactly on every platform. Orca's `MessageDialog` remains\nthe rule for genuinely native prompts, and `wxMessageBox` is never used (memory: `use-orca-messagedialog`). Every\ncolour and size in the native rows comes from `ShellTheme` and the tokens.\n\n### 5.4 Optional seam: keep the test valid after a reload\n\nFact 2 means a reopened test is a plain tower. Two ways out, pick after measuring: (a) a workspace fact\n`calibration.generatedThisSession` the skill reads, plus board 7's regenerate offer; or (b) store the `Calib_Params`\nwith the fork's own project data (`Agent/ProjectPersistence`) and re-apply `set_calib_params` on the plate's print\nafter load. (b) removes board 7's warning entirely and is small if the load observer in `Workspace/FileLoads` can\nrun it; the preset edits already come back with the project. The PA pattern's custom G-code needs nothing.\n\n## 6. Verification required before calling it done\n\n- Adapter test (Catch2, `tests/workspace`): generate each of the three tests from a project with unsaved preset\n  edits; assert a version was saved first, the new project is named, the plate holds the test objects, and the\n  print's `calib_params` match the request. Then reload the saved test and assert what fact 2 says, or what seam\n  (b) fixes.\n- Settings test: a preview with `persistAs` on a stock filament reports `read_only_preset` with the copy name;","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"26cc4316-a2e5-421e-ba0f-88131be8727a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:01:41.905Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 3. Facts verified in the code (read, not run)\n\n1. **Every OrcaSlicer generator replaces the open project and edits project-wide presets.** `Plater::calib_pa`,\n   `calib_temp`, `calib_flowrate`, `calib_max_vol_speed`, `calib_retraction`, `calib_VFA`, the input-shaping pair and\n   `Calib_Cornering` (`src/slic3r/GUI/Plater.cpp` from about line 12677) each call `new_project()` and then write to\n   `preset_bundle->prints/filaments/printers.get_edited_preset().config`. Plates have no presets of their own, so a\n   test on a plate of an existing project would change every other plate. Do not try.\n2. **The test's parameters are runtime-only.** The generator stores them on the current plate's `Print` with\n   `set_calib_params` (`Print.hpp:1089`); `GCode.cpp` reads them per layer (temperature at line 4697). Nothing writes\n   them to the 3MF, and loading a project resets the mode to none at `Plater.cpp:5891`. A saved temperature tower,\n   reopened, slices as a plain tower at one temperature. The pressure-advance pattern is the exception: its per-layer\n   commands go into the plate's custom G-code, which the 3MF does save. The PA pattern also hard-codes the first\n   plate's origin (`Plater.cpp:12814`).\n3. **OrcaSlicer already treats one outcome as a new preset.** The Bambu wizard's save page writes flow results as a\n   filament preset named \"<filament> Flow Rate Calibrated\" (`CalibrationWizardSavePage.cpp:37`). Its pressure-advance\n   results go to the machine, not a preset. The SoftFever dialogs (`calib_dlg.cpp`) save nothing: the person types\n   the value into a preset by hand.\n4. **Saving a copy already exists and selects the copy.** `settings_apply_patch` with `persistAs` saves through\n   Orca's own `Tab::save_preset` and asserts the copy is now selected\n   (`Workspace/OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:3356-3369`); the result carries `saved_as`. A stock preset cannot be\n   overwritten and the preview says so with `read_only_preset` and a suggested copy name (`check_persist`, line\n(`Dialog` in `AgentUI/src/components/ChatNavigation.tsx`, `.chat-dialog` in `styles.css`): a web dialog, not\nOrca's `MessageDialog` and not a new native dialog. Kenneth decided this on 2026-10-21 (relayed from the\nplacement-brainstorm session) so that board 3 is matched exactly on every platform. Orca's `MessageDialog` remains\nthe rule for genuinely native prompts, and `wxMessageBox` is never used (memory: `use-orca-messagedialog`). Every\ncolour and size in the native rows comes from `ShellTheme` and the tokens.\n\n### 5.4 Optional seam: keep the test valid after a reload\n\nFact 2 means a reopened test is a plain tower. Two ways out, pick after measuring: (a) a workspace fact\n`calibration.generatedThisSession` the skill reads, plus board 7's regenerate offer; or (b) store the `Calib_Params`\nwith the fork's own project data (`Agent/ProjectPersistence`) and re-apply `set_calib_params` on the plate's print\nafter load. (b) removes board 7's warning entirely and is small if the load observer in `Workspace/FileLoads` can\nrun it; the preset edits already come back with the project. The PA pattern's custom G-code needs nothing.\n\n## 6. Verification required before calling it done\n\n- Adapter test (Catch2, `tests/workspace`): generate each of the three tests from a project with unsaved preset\n  edits; assert a version was saved first, the new project is named, the plate holds the test objects, and the\n  print's `calib_params` match the request. Then reload the saved test and assert what fact 2 says, or what seam\n  (b) fixes.\n- Settings test: a preview with `persistAs` on a stock filament reports `read_only_preset` with the copy name;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"70596c2c-8c45-46c2-addd-015147fb61d9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":