{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01HtB7VeNGPRuA7KgRBBC6gF","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46"}
{"parentUuid":"a93bc80f-e746-459d-a61f-e9fd0c277372","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31b05e56-dc9c-4fee-8c21-22f2e308b592","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"The user answered: \"A saved calibration test loses its per-block steps when reopened (OrcaSlicer keeps them only in memory). Which way should JusPrin handle it?\"=\"Build board 7 as drawn\", \"If board 7 is built as drawn: its two choices are a primary button and a link, while boards 2, 4 and 6 draw the Agent's choices as reply chips. How should \"Regenerate tower\" and \"Just look at it\" work?\"=\"Correction to calibration-handoff.md, canvas board 7 (\"The test project, reopened later\"):\n\nBoard 7 draws \"Regenerate tower\" as a primary button and \"Just look at it\" as a link under the agent's words. That is a drawing mistake. Build them as Chat/Reply Choice chips, exactly like the choices on boards 2, 4 and 6.\n\nA reply chip sends its text as the person's message. So \"Regenerate tower\" is a reply the agent answers by calling calibration_generate again with the same test and range; \"Just look at it\" is a reply the agent answers by leaving the project as it is. No new control, no button handling in the thread.\n\nThe rule to keep: buttons inside the thread exist only on cards the app draws from tool results (the save proposal on board 5, the receipt on board 6). An agent turn offers choices only as reply chips.\n\nThe board will be redrawn to match; the handoff text takes precedence over the current drawing.\". Read the answers carefully — they may request clarification, changes, or that you not proceed — and follow what they actually say.","tool_use_id":"toolu_018Z8ZztLjTgJhY27szem8uj"}]},"uuid":"6276f03e-291c-4f59-b39c-7625eee44acd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:11:02.444Z","toolUseResult":{"questions":[{"header":"Reopened test","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"Handoff 5.4 option (b): the app stores the test's steps with the project and puts them back on the plate when it reopens, so the tower slices and prints correctly. Board 7's warning, Out of date state and Regenerate button are then never needed; the reopened chat just carries on. Smaller to build, and nobody can print a useless tower.","label":"Keep the steps (Recommended)"},{"description":"Handoff 5.4 option (a): the app records the test (range, date, saved result) with the project; on reopen the card reads Out of date with \"Temperature steps not kept in the file\", the chat opens with \"Opened from Home · generated 21 Oct 2026 · result 225 °C saved\", and the Agent offers Regenerate tower / Just look at it.","label":"Build board 7 as drawn"}],"question":"A saved calibration test loses its per-block steps when reopened (OrcaSlicer keeps them only in memory). Which way should JusPrin handle it?"},{"header":"Buttons","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"The app draws them under the Agent's message: Regenerate tower makes the test again with the recorded range (after the board 3 confirmation), Just look at it closes the offer. Works the same whatever the model writes.","label":"App buttons, as drawn"},{"description":"The Agent's Choices line, drawn as reply chips like the other boards; pressing one sends it as your reply and the Agent acts on it. Differs from the board's look.","label":"Reply chips"},{"description":"Only matters if board 7 is built as drawn.","label":"Not applicable"}],"question":"If board 7 is built as drawn: its two choices are a primary button and a link, while boards 2, 4 and 6 draw the Agent's choices as reply chips. How should \"Regenerate tower\" and \"Just look at it\" work?"}],"answers":{"A saved calibration test loses its per-block steps when reopened (OrcaSlicer keeps them only in memory). Which way should JusPrin handle it?":"Build board 7 as drawn","If board 7 is built as drawn: its two choices are a primary button and a link, while boards 2, 4 and 6 draw the Agent's choices as reply chips. How should \"Regenerate tower\" and \"Just look at it\" work?":"Correction to calibration-handoff.md, canvas board 7 (\"The test project, reopened later\"):\n\nBoard 7 draws \"Regenerate tower\" as a primary button and \"Just look at it\" as a link under the agent's words. That is a drawing mistake. Build them as Chat/Reply Choice chips, exactly like the choices on boards 2, 4 and 6.\n\nA reply chip sends its text as the person's message. So \"Regenerate tower\" is a reply the agent answers by calling calibration_generate again with the same test and range; \"Just look at it\" is a reply the agent answers by leaving the project as it is. No new control, no button handling in the thread.\n\nThe rule to keep: buttons inside the thread exist only on cards the app draws from tool results (the save proposal on board 5, the receipt on board 6). An agent turn offers choices only as reply chips.\n\nThe board will be redrawn to match; the handoff text takes precedence over the current drawing."}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a93bc80f-e746-459d-a61f-e9fd0c277372","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_temporary"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration\\src\\slic3r\\GUI\\JusPrin","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"claude/calibration","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
