 at one setting, and offer to make it again with the same range. End with \"Choices: Regenerate tower | Just look at it\". On \"Regenerate tower\", call calibration_generate with the same test, range and project name: that reply is the go-ahead, since the person agreed to the test when it was first made. On \"Just look at it\", leave the project as it is. Otherwise, while the plate carries calibration, its steps are in place. A flow test keeps its tiles' ratios and the pressure-advance pattern its G-code; neither needs anything.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"The app's note says when the person saved it, and under what name. Say the preset's name exactly\"\"\",\n\"\"\"The app's note says when the person saved it, and under what name. Call setup_record with the same purpose and the range followed by the result as the headline, such as \"230 → 190 °C in 5 °C blocks; result 215 °C saved\", so the test's card keeps it. Say the preset's name exactly\"\"\"),\n])\nedit(\"skills.test.ts\", [\n(\"\"\"    expect(text).toContain('offer to make it again with the same range');\"\"\",\n\"\"\"    expect(text).toContain('offer to make it again with the same range');\n    expect(text).toContain('\"Choices: Regenerate tower | Just look at it\"');\n    expect(text).toContain('\"230 → 190 °C in 5 °C blocks; result 215 °C saved\"');\"\"\"),\n])\nprint(\"ok\")\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"73eee741-3efb-4536-aac6-3635d1790fcb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration\\src\\slic3r\\GUI\\JusPrin\\AgentUI","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"claude/calibration","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
