{"parentUuid":"27686cb7-f451-422f-94a9-c09745ce6521","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHofznCe7JoGwLCqE1B8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SMqE2Ctt7WwoymsM7g1SLz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/src/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/calibration && cp /c/b/cal-capture23/11-reopened.png calibration-review/board-check/v97-07-app-reopened.png && cp \"/c/Users/guitest/.claude/projects/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/tool-results/REDACTED.jpg\" calibration-review/board-check/v97-07-board-7.jpg && git add src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin tests/agent tests/jusprin_support tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp && cat > /c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad/msg-board7.txt <<'EOF'\nWarn when a calibration test is reopened without its steps\n\nBoard 7: OrcaSlicer keeps a test's per-block steps only in memory, so a\nreopened temperature tower (or pressure-advance tower or line) would slice\nat one setting. The project's document now keeps the test the in-app Agent\nmade: test, method, range, when it was generated, and the result once the\nperson saves one (Undo clears it). When a project's document comes in and\nit is such a test whose plate holds no steps, the chat gets the app's line\n(\"Opened from Home · generated 22 Oct 2026 · result 215 °C saved\"), the\nmodel reads a fuller version of it (ConversationMessage::for_model), and\nits turn offers \"Choices: Regenerate tower | Just look at it\" as reply\nchips, per Kenneth's correction to the board. The setup card reads Out of\ndate with \"Temperature steps not kept in the file\" in its attention block.\n\nHome tells the host a project was opened from it. Undo on a reopened test\ndrops the copy's loaded edits before switching back, as printer setup\ndoes, so OrcaSlicer's modal never asks. The skill records the result in\nthe setup headline and words the reopened offer. The fake's generated\nplate carries its steps, as the adapter's does. The calibration capture\nnow leaves the test, reopens it from Home, and undoes the save there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git commit -q -F /c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad/msg-board7.txt </dev/null 2>/dev/null; git log --oneline -1; git status --short","description":"Save review images and commit board 7"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_read_input_tokens":494967,"output_tokens":1230,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":208},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1230,"cache_read_input_tokens":494967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SMqE2Ctt7WwoymsM7g1SLz":{"command":"cd /c/src/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/calibration && cp /c/b/cal-capture23/11-reopened.png calibration-review/board-check/v97-07-app-reopened.png && cp \"/c/Users/guitest/.claude/projects/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/tool-results/REDACTED.jpg\" calibration-review/board-check/v97-07-board-7.jpg && git add src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin tests/agent tests/jusprin_support tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp && cat > /c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad/msg-board7.txt <<'EOF'\nWarn when a calibration test is reopened without its steps\n\nBoard 7: OrcaSlicer keeps a test's per-block steps only in memory, so a\nreopened temperature tower (or pressure-advance tower or line) would slice\nat one setting. The project's document now keeps the test the in-app Agent\nmade: test, method, range, when it was generated, and the result once the\nperson saves one (Undo clears it). When a project's document comes in and\nit is such a test whose plate holds no steps, the chat gets the app's line\n(\"Opened from Home · generated 22 Oct 2026 · result 215 °C saved\"), the\nmodel reads a fuller version of it (ConversationMessage::for_model), and\nits turn offers \"Choices: Regenerate tower | Just look at it\" as reply\nchips, per Kenneth's correction to the board. The setup card reads Out of\ndate with \"Temperature steps not kept in the file\" in its attention block.\n\nHome tells the host a project was opened from it. Undo on a reopened test\ndrops the copy's loaded edits before switching back, as printer setup\ndoes, so OrcaSlicer's modal never asks. The skill records the result in\nthe setup headline and words the reopened offer. The fake's generated\nplate carries its steps, as the adapter's does. The calibration capture\nnow leaves the test, reopens it from Home, and undoes the save there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git commit -q -F /c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad/msg-board7.txt </dev/null 2>/dev/null; git log --oneline -1; git status --short","description":"Save review images and commit board 7"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgHofzUbE7RhJhfATd7hF","requestRef":"e50ab41e-77f3-4e52-ac8f-7fa564bea659","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3dcaa3a-a125-405a-ad87-204d1051f02f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T19:11:38.443Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPr