{"parentUuid":"9e597ac6-1dd3-4034-b3fd-2e20673efdea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHop9xKjyLu6UAWUi1XT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Board 7 now matches, with the two choices drawn as reply chips per your correction. The images above show the board on the left and the app after reopening the test from Home on the right.\n\n**What a reopened test looks like**\n- The setup card reads **Out of date**, with \"Temperature steps not kept in the file\" in its warning area.\n- Its headline keeps the result: \"230 → 190 °C in 5 °C blocks; result 215 °C saved\". The Agent now writes that headline after a save.\n- The chat opens with the board's line: \"Opened from Home · generated 22 Oct 2026 · result 215 °C saved\". If the project wasn't opened from Home, it starts with \"Reopened\" instead.\n- The Agent explains that slicing now would print the whole tower at 230 °C. It offers **Regenerate tower** and **Just look at it** as reply chips. The skill tells it to make the test again with the same range when you pick Regenerate.\n- The pressure-advance pattern and flow tests keep what they need in the file, so they never get this warning.\n\n**How it works**\n- When the Agent makes a test, the app now saves it with the project: the test, its range, when it was made, and the result once you save one. Undo clears the result.\n- When a project like that is reopened and its plate has lost the steps, the app posts the line and the Agent replies.\n\n**Differences from the board**\n- The card says \"Not sliced yet\" where the board shows 48 min / 11 g, only because the harness never sliced the tower.\n- Temperatures show OrcaSlicer's own \"℃\" sign, as on boards 5 and 6, where the board writes \"°C\".\n\n**Found and fixed along the way**\n- Undo on a reopened test froze the app on an OrcaSlicer prompt about unsaved filament changes. A reopened project loads the test's own edits onto the saved copy, so OrcaSlicer asks before switching.\n- Undo now drops those edits first, the same way the fork's printer setup already does, so nothing asks.\n- The capture run covers the whole path: leave the test, reopen it from Home, then Undo. Every check passes.\n\n**Checks**\n- New card and record tests pass.\n- The full suites show only the old line-ending failures. Three MCP bridge tests failed once while the machine was busy and passed when rerun on their own.\n- I didn't rerun the adapter harness or the default shell harness for this change. I also didn't add an automated test for reopening outside the shell harness; the real-app capture run is what checks that path.\n- The skill changed again, so its recorded prompt tests still need re-recording. I haven't run any live model.\n\nCommitted as a1f841126c, not pushed.\n\nDoes board 7 match, so I can move on to board 8 (Home)?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":951,"cache_read_input_tokens":497570,"output_tokens":884,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":951,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":497570,"cache_creation_input_tokens":951,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":951},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgHop9dEtAJxWJVhnuGX7","requestRef":"8e5a45c6-311b-4ee6-afb1-b9069ed6c598","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"342bd3bf-ca5f-4df9-9d10-ac1fc2af5a1a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T19:13:25.328Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-