{"parentUuid":"39a4e30d-c5c9-4a3e-9456-41f629e4e918","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8bcbaeb6-a8ca-4f4c-93f9-6209a8f6bef9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"The user answered: \"Board 8 shows Backpack hook's card as \"Sliced, ready · Gray PETG\". Today every Home project card says just \"Saved\", and Home doesn't know a closed project's slice state or filament. Should this calibration work also change every project card's status line?\"=\"No. Calibration does not change Home's project cards. Home knows a closed project only by its name, its thumbnail and whether a print is running: OrcaHomeBackend.cpp (around line 202) sets \"Printing\" from the ledger and \"Saved\" for everything else, and it does not know a closed project's slice state or filament. Board 8 was wrong and has been redrawn: both cards read \"Saved\", and the test is told apart by its project name, \"Temperature tower · Gray PETG\". Its result lives in the test project's own chat and receipt.\n\nSo: do not add slice state, filament or the calibration result to project cards, and do not touch the Home backend's status logic. Whether a card could one day carry a calibration result is a Home gallery decision, outside this work. The handoff's section 4 (board 8 line) says the same.\". Read the answers carefully — they may request clarification, changes, or that you not proceed — and follow what they actually say.","tool_use_id":"toolu_019y2eVxsAJSTXMU7QVV8yH5"}]},"uuid":"3e0ddeff-aefa-48b3-87b3-4782717ad839","timestamp":"2026-10-22T19:37:41.874Z","toolUseResult":{"questions":[{"header":"Home cards","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"The test's card reads \"Saved <preset>\" in the success colour, from the result the test project keeps. Every other card keeps \"Saved\" as today, so Backpack hook won't show \"Sliced, ready · Gray PETG\". The general status line can be its own piece of Home work.","label":"Only the test card (Recommended)"},{"description":"Also give every project card a status from its saved state: \"Sliced, ready\" or not, plus its first filament, read from each project's stored version without opening it. A larger change to Home, outside calibration.","label":"Build both lines"}],"question":"Board 8 shows Backpack hook's card as \"Sliced, ready · Gray PETG\". Today every Home project card says just \"Saved\", and Home doesn't know a closed project's slice state or filament. Should this calibration work also change every project card's status line?"}],"answers":{"Board 8 shows Backpack hook's card as \"Sliced, ready · Gray PETG\". Today every Home project card says just \"Saved\", and Home doesn't know a closed project's slice state or filament. Should this calibration work also change every project card's status line?":"No. Calibration does not change Home's project cards. Home knows a closed project only by its name, its thumbnail and whether a print is running: OrcaHomeBackend.cpp (around line 202) sets \"Printing\" from the ledger and \"Saved\" for everything else, and it does not know a closed project's slice state or filament. Board 8 was wrong and has been redrawn: both cards read \"Saved\", and the test is told apart by its project name, \"Temperature tower · Gray PETG\". Its result lives in the test project's own chat and receipt.\n\nSo: do not add slice state, filament or the calibration result to project cards, and do not touch the Home backend's status logic. Whether a card could one day carry a calibration result is a Home gallery decision, outside this work. The handoff's section 4 (board 8 line) says the same."}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"39a4e30d-c5c9-4a3e-9456-41f629e4e918","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_temporary"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration\\src\\slic3r\\GUI\\JusPrin","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"claude/calibration","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
