Home\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;flex:none;position:relative;width:650px;height:482px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-16);padding:var(--space-24) var(--space-24) var(--space-24) var(--space-24);align-items:flex-start;background:var(--surface-canvas);overflow:hidden\"><div class=\"section\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;flex:none;align-self:stretch;color:var(--text-primary)\">8 · On Home</div><div class=\"body-small\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;flex:none;align-self:stretch;color:var(--text-secondary)\">The test is an ordinary ProjectCard in the gallery, so it is found, reopened and deleted like any other. Home knows a closed project only by its name, its thumbnail and whether a print is running, so both cards read “Saved”, as every card does today: the test is told apart by its name, and its result lives in its own chat and receipt. Whether a card could carry a calibration result is a Home gallery question, not part of this work.</div><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;flex:none;flex:none;display:flex;gap:var(--space-16);justify-content:flex-start;align-items:flex-start;\"><div data-c=\"ProjectCard\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;flex:none;width:293px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:1px;align-items:flex-start;background:var(--surface-raised);border-radius:var(--radius-large);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-subtle),var(--elevation-subtle);overflow:hidden\"><div data-image=\"placeholder\" data-n=\"thumbnail\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;flex:none;align-self:stretch;height:220px;background:var(--surface-subtle);border-radius:calc(var(--radius-large) - 1px) calc(var(--radius-large) - 1px) 0 0\"></div><div data-n=\"card-footer\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;flex:none;align-self:stretch;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-4);padding:var(--space-12) var(--space-12) var(--space-12) var(--space-12);align-items:flex-start;overflow:hidden\"><div class=\"body-bold\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;flex:none;align-self: