{"parentUuid":"2daf07ed-078b-4a31-b16b-4fc4ec95b8f8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8bcbaeb6-a8ca-4f4c-93f9-6209a8f6bef9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DcGfJ8Fi5qtwvkuonXk9Pz","type":"tool_result","content":"src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/skills/calibration/SKILL.md:2\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/skills.test.ts:0\ntests/shell/shell_harness.cpp:1\ntests/project_prompt/script.json:1\ntests/project_prompt/requests.json:7\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/skills/calibration/SKILL.md:37:Read the printer, the filament preset and its material from the workspace. Ranges below are mine, and calibration_generate refuses one outside what I accept. Name the test's project after the test and the filament with projectName, such as \"Temperature test · Gray PETG\".\nsrc/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/skills/calibration/SKILL.md:52:The test's project opens with the app's note of the project it started from. What I made is in the workspace: the plate's calibration carries the test and its range, and the objects are the test pieces. In that turn, call setup_record with the test as the purpose (such as \"Temperature test for Bambu PLA Basic\") and the range as the headline. Then tell the person to slice and print it as usual, what to photograph and how, and to send the photo here.\n1112:                    m_notebook->GetSelection() == MainFrame::tpHome; }, \"stock_startup_ready\",\n2638:        m_frame->select_tab(size_t(MainFrame::tpHome));\n4723:        return m_notebook->GetSelection() == MainFrame::tpHome && installed_shell()->home_view()->IsShown() &&\n3702-                                [this] { return !live_panel()->IsShown() && installed_shell()->home_view()->IsShown(); },\n3703-                                [this] {\n3704-                                    for (int settle = 0; settle < 20; ++settle) {\n3705-                                        wxYield();\n3706-                                        wxMilliSlee