{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","hash":"19b9e329ecfd66dbf3672c2afddd6e6128353ee24c9e6446e59510acca9df73e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Same 7 failures as the baseline, so nothing new broke in the default run. Committing the autosave fix and the board 8 changes separately."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R5o2b4eFxHrunLkJNNCRJt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/src/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/calibration && cp /c/b/cal-capture25/13-home.png calibration-review/board-check/v97-08-app-home.png && S=/c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad && cat > $S/msg-autosave.txt <<'EOF'\nKeep a reopened project's name when it saves a new version\n\nA version took its first object's name whenever OrcaSlicer's own project\nname read Untitled, even when the store had already named the project. A\nproject reopened from Home reads Untitled in OrcaSlicer, so its first edit\nafter the reopen renamed it on Home: a calibration test became\n\"temperature_tower\", the generator's object. The object's name is now the\nfallback only for a project with no name yet (empty, or stored as\nUntitled before its first object arrived).\n\nChecked with the calibration capture (reopen, edit, Home) and the default\nshell harness, whose failures are the 7 it had before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit add src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Workspace/ProjectAutosave.cpp && GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git commit -q -F $S/msg-autosave.txt </dev/null 2>/dev/null; cat > $S/msg-board8.txt <<'EOF'\nName a temperature test \"Temperature tower · <filament>\", as the boards do\n\nBoard 8: the test is an ordinary project on Home, told apart by its name;\nits card reads \"Saved\" like every other, and Home is unchanged. The skill's\nexamples now follow the boards' wording for the project and its purpose,\nand the calibration capture ends on Home, checking the test's card.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit add src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/skills/calibration/SKILL.md tests/shell/shell_harness.cpp && GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git commit -q -F $S/msg-board8.txt </dev/null 2>/dev/null; git log --oneline -3; git status --short","description":"Commit the autosave fix and board 8"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
