{"parentUuid":"5b9ca2bb-9d0f-4c61-9a2a-91f75de49722","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHrcvk89CqbgvMcz2mG5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Board 8 matches the redrawn board. The image above is Home after the test: both cards read \"Saved\", and the test is told apart only by its name.\n\n**What changed for board 8**\n- Home's cards and backend are untouched, as you said.\n- The only app change is the skill's naming examples, which now follow the boards. The test project is named like \"Temperature tower · Gray PETG\", and its purpose like \"Temperature tower, Gray PETG on MK4\".\n- The capture run now ends on Home and checks the test's card.\n\n**A bug found and fixed along the way (separate commit, 9e6593b249)**\n- The test's card first showed up on Home as \"temperature_tower\".\n- The cause wasn't calibration. A project reopened from Home reads \"Untitled\" inside OrcaSlicer, so the next time it saved a version, the autosave renamed it after its first object, even though it already had a name. So any reopened project lost its Home name after its next edit. Undo after the reopen triggered it here.\n- That autosave code belongs to the fork, not upstream OrcaSlicer. It now falls back to the object's name only when a project has no name yet, so a new project still gets named after its first model.\n\n**Checks**\n- The calibration capture runs through all eight boards in the real app with every check passing.\n- The default shell harness shows exactly the 7 failures it had before this work.\n- The skill changed again, so its recorded prompt tests still need re-recording. I haven't run any live model.\n\nCommitted as d56157f033, not pushed. The app you were testing is still an old build.\n\nDoes board 8 match, or does it need changes?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":538835,"output_tokens":516,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":721,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":516,"cache_read_input_tokens":538835,"cache_creation_input_tokens":721,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":721},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgHrcvPnpEoeEwiS4mVAA","requestRef":"9cfa4904-acc3-4a49-a043-8a011d38949d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"4dbe78c2-7717-4818-9321-100611139bdc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T19:50:12.137Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"claude/calibration","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
