{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","id":"5a4fb6c0-25d4-4aaa-9d6b-544bf0675ab7","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:01:57.960Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"1b72e66683fe732eb9e8e64e0373cde78c676ba53015232e87d25fddb79253d3","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"46b532d1-b6b1-452f-87c7-d4ef0778ab27","keep":983,"tail":["22a168e681aa596f2b1b26b25c95c7ada3886ad4271901d68c29cf01251a82ca","daf285eda6b3d3ca088d89a565bf50d0c6fb7a21ed2ea184d8fae3591441a747","959cdc1f4c1d2d0ce71ebde9b0a202fea4bc8e844d790447cf7bdfbf0617416e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",985,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"140110cbb3eeeab2fe5a4e8219f1b54879166018b6dd9eac779f280f0a3f62e5"}
{"parentUuid":"59d74dc5-28ab-461d-855a-7d3a63fa5c61","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJW8Tpmsv84oKp1Uv9uQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've re-read the handoff in full, the verification report, and boards 2, 3 and 4 at version 114, and checked their claims against this branch. Most of boards 5–8 survives; the entry flow and the generate tool need rework; and there are eight places where the handoff disagrees with the code or with your earlier answers. No code has changed.\n\n## Survives as built\n\n- **Boards 5–8.** The Save preset card, the receipt with Undo, the reopened-test warning, the test record kept with the project, and the Home rename fix. These don't depend on how the project is created.\n- **The three Calibrate… rows and the hidden Orca Calibration menu.**\n- **The web confirmation dialog**, on both the Agent page and Home. Only its words change, and its button becomes \"Start\".\n- **Notes drawn as a one-line system line.**\n- **Hiding the generator's model load.** The adapter already runs the generator inside `ToolLoad`, so the temperature tower's model load isn't reported as a file the person opened. The verification report saw that file-report note; this branch doesn't produce it.\n- **Release hook skip.** The release hook already skips its save while a generator runs. That's the handoff's 5.1 point 2, already in place.\n- **Treating the generator's edits as the project's starting content.**\n\n## Needs rework\n\n- **What happens after Start.** Today, Start posts a message in the person's voice and the Agent asks which test from the old project's chat. Instead, the app will create the empty \"Calibration · …\" project, mark it as one, post the handover line, and start the first turn with the new `calibration_started` trigger. That trigger also has to be added on the host side.\n- **`calibration_generate`.**\n  - It no longer takes a project name.\n  - It keeps the project and its chat instead of starting a new one, through the one-shot \"continue this project\" switch in `ProjectPersistence`.\n  - It creates the calibration project itself when called from the person's own project.\n  - It returns the new `sessionId`.\n- **Naming the project after generating.** Today this uses a small forwarder I added to OrcaSlicer's `Plater` (`set_project_name`). OrcaSlicer's existing public `set_project_filename` does the job, so I can remove my change, and with it the branch's only change to OrcaSlicer-owned code.\n- **What the host does after a test is made.** Today it posts the opening line into a fresh chat, renames that chat, and starts a turn there. That becomes the handover line plus an exemption so the result lands in the chat that asked.\n- **The skill.** It gets the trigger, asks \"which test?\" only when the handover doesn't decide it, and generates before changing any setting. It drops `projectName`, since the app now names the project.\n- **The shell harness** (boards 2–4) **and the recorded prompt tests.**\n\n## Where the handoff disagrees with the code or with earlier decisions\n\n1. **The Agent's turn would be cut off at the boundary.** Section 5.1 keeps the document across the generator's new project. But adopting a document at a project boundary also tells the host the document was replaced, and the host then:\n   - cancels the Agent's turn,\n   - clears all tool calls, including the generate call that's still running (the same situation that crashed the app earlier, fixed in be98979009),\n   - and drops the turn's pending tool results.\n\n   So the generate result would never reach the model, and board 4's \"Worked for 4s · 2 actions\" can't happen. The one-shot has to skip that notification as well, not only the session check at line ~725 that 5.1 mentions.\n2. **Saving a result.** Section 5.2 point 7 still says the Agent previews and then applies with `persistAs`. Under your board 5 decision the Agent only previews, the app saves on Save preset, and the Agent's own save is refused.\n3. **Questions listed as open that you've already answered:**\n   - Q1: if the person is on their own preset, ask them whether to write into it or save a copy (2026-10-21).\n   - Q2: the tool is offered over MCP too (2026-10-21). Section 5.1 now says in-app only. Which should hold?\n   - Q3: option (a), board 7 as drawn (2026-10-22).\n4. **Three different names for the same test:**\n   - the project: \"Calibration · <filament> · <printer>\" (sections 5.1 and 5.3);\n   - the Home card on board 8: \"Temperature tower · Gray PETG\", which I built into the skill yesterday;\n   - the chat title on board 4: \"Calibrating Gray PETG on MK4\".\n\n   I'd use the project name everywhere, including the chat title. Board 8's card would then read \"Calibration · Gray PETG · Prusa MK4\".\n5. **Handover wording.** Section 5.3 says \"Started from <project> · calibrating <filament> on <printer> · the test's settings are temporary\". Board 4 and your message say \"From <project> · <filament> on <printer> · temporary test settings\". I'd use the board's wording.\n6. **Which chat gets the generate result on the symptom path.** Section 5.1 point 4 says the person's chat keeps the last word. Section 6 says the calibration project's chat holds the handover line and the tool's result. A tool call belongs to one chat. I'd keep the result in the person's chat, as `project_open` does today, and open the calibration chat with the handover line. Relatedly, the handover should name the symptom, but the tool has no symptom input. I'd add an optional `symptom` argument that the Agent fills from the person's words.\n7. **The Home card path doesn't know the filament.** The popup names a filament and the project is named after one, but a Home printer card knows only its printer. Today the Agent sets that printer up, and picks a filament, inside the test project. The handoff doesn't say which filament the app should use, or that the app now has to set that printer up in the new project itself. I'd use the printer's own default filament, or its first loaded spool when the printer reports one.\n8. **The cited naming lines changed.** The report cites `ProjectAutosave.cpp:515-519`, and my fix yesterday changed those lines. Under the new flow the project already has its name when it's created, so the saved name survives either way. Renaming after generating is still needed for OrcaSlicer's title bar.\n\nThe no-agent case is understood: I'll leave the rows enabled and build nothing new for it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":559,"cache_read_input_tokens":605357,"output_tokens":2086,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":559,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2086,"cache_read_input_tokens":605357,"cache_creation_input_tokens":559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":559},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgJW8TShX6Mv99v6pyfCf","requestRef":"5a4fb6c0-25d4-4aaa-9d6b-544bf0675ab7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"34d17de4-0014-414a-967f-4de7461b42a7","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:02:22.843Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
