{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"7d739b50-2878-48fb-9fbb-4ea9fd218752","snapshotMessageId":"14b7bae4-9127-46ef-9ed4-10d83247d5f9","trackingPath":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--src-JusPrin\\e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258\\scratchpad\\edit_r11_guide.py","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-10-23T05:17:24.325Z","realParentDir":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--src-JusPrin\\e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258\\scratchpad"},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T05:17:24.994Z"}
{"parentUuid":"02e6b9f3-51a6-46b9-929c-91b290f5b947","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJbroJJHMTdWtpVrvP9y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fp9L1sayG6NYCe7A4YjAzq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--src-JusPrin\\e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258\\scratchpad\\edit_r11_guide.py","content":"import os\nos.chdir(r\"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration\")\n\n\ndef edit(path, pairs):\n    raw = open(path, \"rb\").read().decode(\"utf-8\")\n    nl = \"\\r\\n\" if \"\\r\\n\" in raw else \"\\n\"\n    s = raw.replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\")\n    for o, n in pairs:\n        assert s.count(o) == 1, (path, o[:70])\n        s = s.replace(o, n)\n    open(path, \"wb\").write(s.replace(\"\\n\", nl).encode(\"utf-8\"))\n\n\nedit(\"agent-docs/jusprin/mcp-tool-extension-guide.md\", [\n(\"\"\"One skill has a description: `calibration`, read when a print problem may come from the filament or its settings, when the person asks to calibrate, or in a calibration test's project; it carries the conversation of a calibration (when a test is worth it, the two facts said before the open project closes, per-test ranges and how to read the print, the naming rule for the saved preset), while `calibration_generate`'s description keeps only that tool's rules. Four skills have triggers, one file each:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"One skill has a description and a trigger: `calibration`, read when a print problem may come from the filament or its settings, when the person asks to calibrate, or in a calibration project, and fired by `calibration_started` on the first turn of a calibration project's chat; it carries the conversation of a calibration (when a test is worth it, the two facts said before the person's project closes, asking which test only when the handover leaves it open, per-test ranges and how to read the print, the naming rule for the saved preset), while `calibration_generate`'s description keeps only that tool's rules. Four other skills have triggers, one file each:\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"| `calibration` | 1 | Calibration tests, each a project of its own. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `calibration` | 1 | Calibration tests, each made in a calibration project of its own. |\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"| `calibration_generate` | M | Implemented, in-app and over MCP. Replace the open project with one of OrcaSlicer's calibration tests (temperature, flow, pressure advance) as a project of its own: Orca's generators call `new_project()` and edit the project-wide presets, so a test cannot be a plate of another project. The open project is first released through `project_open`'s path (saved to its version history, unsaved preset edits dropped); a range Orca's dialog refuses is refused before anything closes. Returns the plate, its objects and the range applied, read back from the plate's print, and a summary sentence; for the in-app Agent the test's project opens its chat with it. The per-layer steps are runtime-only in Orca, so each plate reports them as `calibration` while its print holds them. Analysis is reasoning over a photo; a result is saved with `settings_apply_patch` on the filament scope with `persistAs`, a named copy no other project is switched to. | `Plater::calib_temp`, `calib_flowrate`, `calib_pa` | 64 objects |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `calibration_generate` | M | Implemented, in-app and over MCP. Makes one of OrcaSlicer's calibration tests (temperature, flow, pressure advance) in a calibration project: Orca's generators call `new_project()` and edit the project-wide presets, so a test cannot be a plate of another project. One rule for every path: in a calibration project (the one the Calibrate… rows open) the test is made in it, and the project keeps its identity, chat and name across the generator's own `new_project()` (a one-shot continuation in `ProjectPersistence`; the release hook does not save; the name is put back with `Plater::set_project_filename`); the call takes the session it made, so its result lands in the chat that asked. From any other project it first releases that project through `project_open`'s path (saved to its version history, unsaved preset edits dropped) and opens the calibration project \"Calibration · <filament> · <printer>\" with its handover line, an optional `symptom` naming what the person saw; that chat's first turn starts once the test is made, and the call stays with the project it closed. A range Orca's dialog refuses is refused before anything closes. Returns the project's name, the plate, its objects and the range applied, read back from the plate's print, a summary sentence and the new session. The per-layer steps are runtime-only in Orca, so each plate reports them as `calibration` while its print holds them. Analysis is reasoning over a photo; a result is proposed with `settings_preview_patch` and `persistAs` and saved by the person's Save preset on the card the preview draws, a named copy no other project is switched to. | `Plater::calib_temp`, `calib_flowrate`, `calib_pa` | 64 objects |\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"3. The user reports stringing on a Bambu printer. Judge that a temperature tower is worth it, say that the open project will be saved and closed before generating it, read the user's photo, propose a filament temperature, then preview it and apply it with `persistAs` under the calibrated-copy name. Needs `calibration`, the `calibration` skill and the filament scope.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"3. The user reports stringing on a Bambu printer. Judge that a temperature tower is worth it, say that the open project will be saved and closed before generating it, read the user's photo in the calibration project, and propose a filament temperature as a preview with `persistAs` under the calibrated-copy name, which the user saves from its card. Needs `calibration`, the `calibration` skill and the filament scope.\"\"\"),\n])\nprint(\"ok\")\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_read_input_tokens":753626,"output_tokens":2120,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2120,"cache_read_input_tokens":753626,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Fp9L1sayG6NYCe7A4YjAzq":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--src-JusPrin\\e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258\\scratchpad\\edit_r11_guide.py","content":"import os\nos.chdir(r\"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration\")\n\n\ndef edit(path, pairs):\n    raw = open(path, \"rb\").read().decode(\"utf-8\")\n    nl = \"\\r\\n\" if \"\\r\\n\" in raw else \"\\n\"\n    s = raw.replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\")\n    for o, n in pairs:\n        assert s.count(o) == 1, (path, o[:70])\n        s = s.replace(o, n)\n    open(path, \"wb\").write(s.replace(\"\\n\", nl).encode(\"utf-8\"))\n\n\nedit(\"agent-docs/jusprin/mcp-tool-extension-guide.md\", [\n(\"\"\"One skill has a description: `calibration`, read when a print problem may come from the filament or its settings, when the person asks to calibrate, or in a calibration test's project; it carries the conversation of a calibration (when a test is worth it, the two facts said before the open project closes, per-test ranges and how to read the print, the naming rule for the saved preset), while `calibration_generate`'s description keeps only that tool's rules. Four skills have triggers, one file each:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"One skill has a description and a trigger: `calibration`, read when a print problem may come from the filament or its settings, when the person asks to calibrate, or in a calibration project, and fired by `calibration_started` on the first turn of a calibration project's chat; it carries the conversation of a calibration (when a test is worth it, the two facts said before the person's project closes, asking which test only when the handover leaves it open, per-test ranges and how to read the print, the naming rule for the saved preset), while `calibration_generate`'s description keeps only that tool's rules. Four other skills have triggers, one file each:\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"| `calibration` | 1 | Calibration tests, each a project of its own. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `calibration` | 1 | Calibration tests, each made in a calibration project of its own. |\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"| `calibration_generate` | M | Implemented, in-app and over MCP. Replace the open project with one of OrcaSlicer's calibration tests (temperature, flow, pressure advance) as a project of its own: Orca's generators call `new_project()` and edit the project-wide presets, so a test cannot be a plate of another project. The open project is first released through `project_open`'s path (saved to its version history, unsaved preset edits dropped); a range Orca's dialog refuses is refused before anything closes. Returns the plate, its objects and the range applied, read back from the plate's print, and a summary sentence; for the in-app Agent the test's project opens its chat with it. The per-layer steps are runtime-only in Orca, so each plate reports them as `calibration` while its print holds them. Analysis is reasoning over a photo; a result is saved with `settings_apply_patch` on the filament scope with `persistAs`, a named copy no other project is switched to. | `Plater::calib_temp`, `calib_flowrate`, `calib_pa` | 64 objects |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `calibration_generate` | M | Implemented, in-app and over MCP. Makes one of OrcaSlicer's calibration tests (temperature, flow, pressure advance) in a calibration project: Orca's generators call `new_project()` and edit the project-wide presets, so a test cannot be a plate of another project. One rule for every path: in a calibration project (the one the Calibrate… rows open) the test is made in it, and the project keeps its identity, chat and name across the generator's own `new_project()` (a one-shot continuation in `ProjectPersistence`; the release hook does not save; the name is put back with `Plater::set_project_filename`); the call takes the session it made, so its result lands in the chat that asked. From any other project it first releases that project through `project_open`'s path (saved to its version history, unsaved preset edits dropped) and opens the calibration project \"Calibration · <filament> · <printer>\" with its handover line, an optional `symptom` naming what the person saw; that chat's first turn starts once the test is made, and the call stays with the project it closed. A range Orca's dialog refuses is refused before anything closes. Returns the project's name, the plate, its objects and the range applied, read back from the plate's print, a summary sentence and the new session. The per-layer steps are runtime-only in Orca, so each plate reports them as `calibration` while its print holds them. Analysis is reasoning over a photo; a result is proposed with `settings_preview_patch` and `persistAs` and saved by the person's Save preset on the card the preview draws, a named copy no other project is switched to. | `Plater::calib_temp`, `calib_flowrate`, `calib_pa` | 64 objects |\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"3. The user reports stringing on a Bambu printer. Judge that a temperature tower is worth it, say that the open project will be saved and closed before generating it, read the user's photo, propose a filament temperature, then preview it and apply it with `persistAs` under the calibrated-copy name. Needs `calibration`, the `calibration` skill and the filament scope.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"3. The user reports stringing on a Bambu printer. Judge that a temperature tower is worth it, say that the open project will be saved and closed before generating it, read the user's photo in the calibration project, and propose a filament temperature as a preview with `persistAs` under the calibrated-copy name, which the user saves from its card. Needs `calibration`, the `calibration` skill and the filament scope.\"\"\"),\n])\nprint(\"ok\")\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgJbrnwxrXFjchUp4DbqX","requestRef":"2be83f68-adc3-45d2-ab9c-b9f237743afb","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7d739b50-2878-48fb-9fbb-4ea9fd218752","timestamp":"2026-10-23T05:17:24.036Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
