{"parentUuid":"5d653d5a-58b9-4152-b60c-057bb7c70c6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKJPrtsSvwMrT5i8eiYu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019ehReG7EprVrQRVS5vnAFf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A agent-docs src tests && git status --short | grep -v \"^[MA] \" ; S=/c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad; cat > $S/msg-oneflow.txt <<'EOF'\nCalibrate through one popup into a calibration project the test continues\n\nThe revised handoff (2026-10-22): one popup naming the filament and\nprinter, then the app opens an empty calibration project, and the test is\ngenerated into that same project.\n\n- Start (board 3): the app saves and releases the open project through\n  project_open's path, opens \"Calibration · <filament> · <printer>\" (a\n  Home card: \"Calibration · <printer>\", with the card's printer selected\n  and its loaded spools handed over), marks it in the project document,\n  names its chat the same, posts the handover line (\"From <project> ·\n  <filament> on <printer> · temporary test settings\") and starts the\n  first turn with the new calibration_started trigger. Nothing is posted\n  in the person's voice any more.\n- calibration_generate has one rule: in a calibration project the test is\n  made in it; from any other project (the symptom path) the tool releases\n  it, opens the calibration project with an optional symptom, then makes\n  the test. projectName is gone.\n- The project continues across the generator's own new_project():\n  ProjectPersistence::continuing_project keeps the document and does not\n  report it replaced (the host would otherwise cancel the turn and clear\n  the running call), the release hook does not save, and the call takes\n  the session it made so its result lands in the chat that asked. From\n  the symptom path the person's chat keeps the last word and the\n  calibration chat's first turn starts once the test is made.\n- The name is put back with Plater::set_project_name, the forwarder this\n  branch already had: set_project_filename empties a name with \"·\" on\n  Windows (Kenneth chose to keep the forwarder).\n- The skill gains its trigger, asks which test only when the handover\n  leaves it open (and which spool first from a Home card), makes the test\n  before any setting changes, and drops projectName.\n- What a row does with no agent is undecided: it opens the calibration\n  project all the same.\n\nTests: coordinator (both paths, continuation, session), bridge (symptom\npath, popup path continuing the project and chat, Home handover), the\nadapter harness (each test keeps the project id, chat and name, Home count\nunchanged), and the calibration capture through boards 2 to 8.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git commit -q -F $S/msg-oneflow.txt </dev/null 2>/dev/null; git log --oneline -2; git status --short","description":"Commit the one-popup rework"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2534,"cache_read_input_tokens":787042,"output_tokens":1045,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2534,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1045,"cache_read_input_tokens":787042,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2534},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019ehReG7EprVrQRVS5vnAFf":{"command":"cd /c/src/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/calibration && git add -A agent-docs src tests && git status --short | grep -v \"^[MA] \" ; S=/c/Users/guitest/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--src-JusPrin/e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258/scratchpad; cat > $S/msg-oneflow.txt <<'EOF'\nCalibrate through one popup into a calibration project the test continues\n\nThe revised handoff (2026-10-22): one popup naming the filament and\nprinter, then the app opens an empty calibration project, and the test is\ngenerated into that same project.\n\n- Start (board 3): the app saves and releases the open project through\n  project_open's path, opens \"Calibration · <filament> · <printer>\" (a\n  Home card: \"Calibration · <printer>\", with the card's printer selected\n  and its loaded spools handed over), marks it in the project document,\n  names its chat the same, posts the handover line (\"From <project> ·\n  <filament> on <printer> · temporary test settings\") and starts the\n  first turn with the new calibration_started trigger. Nothing is posted\n  in the person's voice any more.\n- calibration_generate has one rule: in a calibration project the test is\n  made in it; from any other project (the symptom path) the tool releases\n  it, opens the calibration project with an optional symptom, then makes\n  the test. projectName is gone.\n- The project continues across the generator's own new_project():\n  ProjectPersistence::continuing_project keeps the document and does not\n  report it replaced (the host would otherwise cancel the turn and clear\n  the running call), the release hook does not save, and the call takes\n  the session it made so its result lands in the chat that asked. From\n  the symptom path the person's chat keeps the last word and the\n  calibration chat's first turn starts once the test is made.\n- The name is put back with Plater::set_project_name, the forwarder this\n  branch already had: set_project_filename empties a name with \"·\" on\n  Windows (Kenneth chose to keep the forwarder).\n- The skill gains its trigger, asks which test only when the handover\n  leaves it open (and which spool first from a Home card), makes the test\n  before any setting changes, and drops projectName.\n- What a row does with no agent is undecided: it opens the calibration\n  project all the same.\n\nTests: coordinator (both paths, continuation, session), bridge (symptom\npath, popup path continuing the project and chat, Home handover), the\nadapter harness (each test keeps the project id, chat and name, Home count\nunchanged), and the calibration capture through boards 2 to 8.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git commit -q -F $S/msg-oneflow.txt </dev/null 2>/dev/null; git log --oneline -2; git status --short","description":"Commit the one-popup rework"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_019ehReG7EprVrQRVS5vnAFf":{"cwd":"/c/src/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/calibration"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgKJPrW4Qc89ikUTV5BpN","requestRef":"ccea5850-f2f5-46af-864b-79716a9a7998","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"99ef5c34-91af-4ade-a1b4-2017f6462170","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:08:53.674Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"claude/calibration","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
