{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","id":"a1fd7d2b-a7f5-4ec1-8264-2507bbe23f72","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:09:25.051Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"1b72e66683fe732eb9e8e64e0373cde78c676ba53015232e87d25fddb79253d3","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"6fd7c230-aca3-4e85-bc47-f222fafe2598","keep":1292,"tail":["61b244a7c66041c896fe4e8e7c1022ecba6bbd8db96fd369eef63474fcfff426","b034265828e46e49a19a209abb882fc319a16de2f90de91321ac255b20c475ba","e37f283dfd50dc885371f3bef7ecfafa07bd3757425a824d3de67cbb812efcfc"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1294,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"b5e1a2bbc7fece2d9dd157b999d723ff59acee25f5dc0861922f4eec6fa7bd47"}
{"parentUuid":"ccc6b0c0-5261-431c-abae-f3fba773ef48","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKJT8reh2S2cMtnEV41V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The one-popup flow is built to your eight answers and committed (0f47168b87), and the full calibration run passes in the real app. The three images above show the popup, the new project asking which test, and the tower made in that same project.\n\n**What happens now**\n- **Calibrate… row:** it shows board 3's popup, \"Calibrate Bambu PLA Basic on Workshop X1C?\", with Cancel and Start. From a Home card it reads \"Calibrate Workshop X1C?\" and names no filament.\n- **On Start, the app (not the Agent):**\n  - saves and closes your project;\n  - opens \"Calibration · Bambu PLA Basic · Workshop X1C\", and gives its chat the same name;\n  - opens the chat with \"From Backpack hook · Bambu PLA Basic on Workshop X1C · temporary test settings\";\n  - starts the Agent's first turn with the calibration skill already active.\n\n  The old line in your voice (\"I'm fine with … being saved and closed\") is gone.\n- **From a Home card:** the app selects that printer, names the project \"Calibration · Workshop X1C\", and tells the Agent which spools the printer reports, so it asks which filament before which test.\n- **Making the test:** the Agent asks which test only when the handover doesn't decide it. The test is then made in the same project and chat. Its result comes back to the turn that asked, which records the test and says what to print. Only one project is added to Home.\n- **The symptom path:** the tool saves your project, opens the calibration project with your symptom handed over, and makes the test there. Your chat ends with your reply, and the calibration chat's first turn starts once the test exists.\n- **No agent set up:** what a row should do is still undecided, so it opens the calibration project the same way.\n\n**The project-name fix needed the forwarder after all**\n- The generator renames the project to its own test name, so the app has to put the calibration project's name back. OrcaSlicer's `set_project_filename` empties any name containing \"·\" on Windows. The handoff's check ran on macOS, where it works.\n- As you chose, the branch keeps the one-line `Plater::set_project_name` forwarder it already had. It's byte-for-byte the same as before, so the earlier no-conflict rebase check still applies.\n\n**Checks**\n- **Real app:** the capture run went from the popup through all of boards 4 to 8. It confirmed the handover line, the project name, the same project and chat before and after making the test, and one project added to Home.\n- **Adapter harness:** all three tests kept the project's identity, chat and name, and the Home count didn't change.\n- **Bridge tests:** these cover the symptom path, the popup path, and the Home card's handover with spools.\n- **Suites:** the agent tests, page tests and default shell harness show only failures that were there before this work.\n\n**Not done or not verified**\n- The recorded prompt tests that section 6 lists (\"which test?\" with and without a handover, the symptom path, the photo turn) haven't been re-recorded for the new flow. No live model was run.\n- I haven't rerun the end-to-end MCP run on the fake printer with the new flow.\n- The handover in the symptom path is covered by bridge tests only; the real-app run doesn't exercise it.\n- Your running app (process 17456) is from this build folder, so I haven't relinked the app. Close it and I can rebuild and launch it.\n- Nothing is pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":597,"cache_read_input_tokens":793129,"output_tokens":1110,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":597,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1110,"cache_read_input_tokens":793129,"cache_creation_input_tokens":597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":597},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgKJT8L9MeKfjc5yUXXNv","requestRef":"a1fd7d2b-a7f5-4ec1-8264-2507bbe23f72","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8af3587-ada2-4c5c-a8e3-d9a876a29092","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:09:38.336Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin\\.claude\\worktrees\\calibration\\calibration-review\\board-check","sessionId":"e7286644-9c40-4163-89b2-1b9685541258","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"claude/calibration","slug":"steady-sparking-swan"}
